From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:03:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: apple: let s2idle use the second T6040 state

T6040 marked its second entry CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF so that only the WFI
entry would run. Both entries are the same WFI here, so the flag
protects nothing, but it disables the entry for s2idle too:
find_deepest_state() skips disabled states, returns the fallback index
0, and cpuidle_enter_s2idle() does nothing. Suspend-to-idle then never
reaches tick_freeze() and timekeeping suspension, which is why T8140
keeps index 1 in the first place.

Drop the flag.

Fixes: 474e2bc3ed ("cpuidle: apple: Add T6040 with the second state off by default")
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit a391e5394aad97ba7ed8924cec4f47eaf078bf72)
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c | 9 ---------
 1 file changed, 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
index ba52a80fbc..7a53c01792 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-apple.c
@@ -136,15 +136,6 @@ static int apple_cpuidle_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8140") || t604x)
 		apple_idle_driver.states[STATE_PWRDOWN] = apple_idle_driver.states[STATE_WFI];
 
-	/*
-	 * T6040 (M4 Pro) is the same: iBoot locks CYC_OVRD, and a plain
-	 * WFI already powers the core down, losing x0-x15 and FP/SIMD
-	 * (the arm64 idle code saves those). Keep the second state off
-	 * until it is enabled through sysfs.
-	 */
-	if (t604x)
-		apple_idle_driver.states[STATE_PWRDOWN].flags |= CPUIDLE_FLAG_OFF;
-
 	return cpuidle_register(&apple_idle_driver, NULL);
 }
 
